diff --git a/docs/versionhistory.rst b/docs/versionhistory.rst
index 98bbb70..ced3a31 100644
--- a/docs/versionhistory.rst
+++ b/docs/versionhistory.rst
@@ -27,6 +27,13 @@ This library adheres to `Semantic Versioning 2.0 <http://semver.org/>`_.
   ``CapacityLimiter.acquire_nowait_on_behalf_of()`` raising ``trio.WouldBlock`` instead
   of ``anyio.WouldBlock`` on the ``trio`` backend when there are no tokens available
   (`#1218 <https://github.com/agronholm/anyio/pull/1218>`_)
+- Fixed ``CapacityLimiter`` on the asyncio backend over-granting tokens when a
+  non-blocking acquire (``acquire_nowait()`` or ``acquire_on_behalf_of_nowait()``) was
+  made in the window between a release and the woken waiter resuming: the freed token
+  was visible as available even though it had already been handed to the waiter,
+  allowing ``borrowed_tokens`` to exceed ``total_tokens`` and ``available_tokens`` to
+  go negative. The token is now reserved for the woken waiter at notification time, so
+  a non-blocking acquire correctly raises ``WouldBlock`` in that window
 
 **4.14.1**
 
